<<~ kanawai "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119">>



<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Ahu

//ahu// — Hawaiian: heap, pile, mound, cairn; altar, shrine; a sacred stone structure.
Used in spiritual and ceremonial contexts — the //ahu// becomes sacred through human intention
and accumulated offering placed upon it. A landmark made from accumulation; addressable because
it has been named and tended.

A child-slot sigil. Each `ahu` block declares a named scope boundary within a meme — an
addressable child tiddler at `parentUri + slot`. The slot name becomes the tiddler title suffix.
Slots compose the structural skeleton of a meme's content; each MAY hold its own TOML meta header (set of tiddler fields)
and wikitext body.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ sense the slot name — a `#/name` anchor, rooted at the carrier; the boundary scope of this content unit
⏿ orient: child-slot, parent-relative addressing; slot name becomes tiddler title suffix
◇ parent at `lar:///uri`; this slot creates child at `lar:///uri#/name`; content stays inside boundary
▶ emit child-slot block node; deserializer produces a separate tiddler for each slot
↺ parent tiddler references child via `<<~ kahea ahu #/name>>`; child is independently addressable; confirm round-trip: parent body contains kahea~ahu summons; child has meta fields + content

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Law (Kānāwai)

An ahu block slot name MUST begin with `#/`. The slash roots the path at the carrier, so a slot names the same string it addresses; a nested slot extends it (`#/parent/child`). A bare `#name` belongs to no ahu slot grammar: a processor MUST preserve that source verbatim, surface a diagnostic to the operator, and MUST NOT normalize it or mint a child address from it. A CONTROL slot carries structural metadata rather than addressable content and takes no root — it opens no child to address.
A slot token admits `[a-z0-9āēīōūʻ-]` — lowercase ASCII letters and digits, a hyphen, the Hawaiian long vowels ā ē ī ō ū (precomposed), and the ʻokina (U+02BB); `/` nests, and `$` is reserved as a leading carriage marker (RULED, operator, slot-grammar-orthography). `lares meme normalize` folds a slot name — and only a slot name, fence-masked — to NFC first (so a decomposed vowel, a base letter plus the combining macron U+0304, precomposes to its canonical letter), then folds the three ʻokina look-alikes (the curly quotes U+2018/U+2019 and the typable straight apostrophe U+0027) to U+02BB, reporting each fold as a diagnostic. Kahakō and ʻokina stand RULED; a kahakō look-alike (a folding macron on any other vowel, or any other Hawaiian orthographic mark) is NOT ruled — it stays unfolded, and MUST pass through unchanged.
An ahu block MUST close with `<<~/ahu>>`.
An ahu block MAY nest inside another ahu block. A nested slot extends its enclosing slot path (`#/parent/child`), while a top-level slot begins a path at the carrier root.
An ahu slot MUST produce an independently addressable tiddler at `parentUri + slot`.
The tiddler representing an enclosing scope MUST reference each child slot via `<<~ kahea ahu #/slot>>` in its body.
Child slot tiddlers MUST NOT duplicate the parent's meta TOML — they carry their own.

The slot name `#/head` is conventional for the meme's primary content body.
The slot name `#source-shelf` is conventional for pranala edge declarations.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/syntax>>

!! Syntax

Decomposed at the wiki's causal island boundaries:

```text
<<~ ahu #/slot-name>>
content body

<<~/ahu>>
```

Compound kahea-ahu summons form (in parent tiddler body after decomposition):
```text
<<~ kahea ahu #/slot-name>>
```

Regex (open, canonical):
```
/<<~[^>]*\bahu\s+(#\/[\w-]+(?:\/[\w-]+)*)\s*>>/
```

Close tag: `<<~/ahu>>`

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/schema>>

!! Schema (machine-readable)

```toml
sigil          = "ahu"
kind           = "child-slot"
layer          = "block"
default-family = null

open-pattern  = '<<~[^>]*\bahu\s+(#\/[\w-]+(?:\/[\w-]+)*)\s*>>'
close-pattern = '<<~\/ahu\s*>>'

[captures]
slot = 1
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/quoteblock-floor>>

!! The quoteblock floor — un-decomposable content fences, never drops

Content that will not decompose fences to a quoteblock. The fence stands as the artifact a writer surfaces to the operator: a demotion, never an overwrite, never a drop.

The grain matches the write that produces the un-decomposable content:

* ''Whole-chunk ingest'' — a carrier arrives through the deserializer, or from outside the wiki into it, whole and partially un-decomposable. The whole chunk quoteblocks; no family stands yet at that point, so the carrier is the only grain available.
* ''In-place ahu update'' — an ahu tiddler that already stands, edited to un-decomposable content. ONLY that ahu's body quoteblocks; the `<<~ ahu #/slot>>…<<~/ahu>>` wrapper survives untouched, and the rest of the family stands untouched. A paste into the live TW5 browser counts as a write: the save lands in the CRDT store, and the house projects it back to disk — so this grain governs there too (fix on write).

A fenced span needs no new law to keep the ahu-fidelity guard honest. Fence-mask covers it (#/syntax, #/schema; the shared scanner at `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-ast/ahu-scan.ts`), so the span declares zero slots, so `collectAhuSlots` finds nothing to drop. Un-decomposable content can never mint a phantom slot or a false conflict — the guard passes by construction.

Quoteblocking runs as a one-way demotion: every sigil inside goes inert until the operator resolves it. The surfacing rail that carries that demotion to the operator is NOT optional — a quoteblock nobody sees reads as a drop wearing a cure's face. Blast radius equals the write's grain: a per-tiddler edit never demotes the whole meme.

A child-slot save re-grades its root through the backstop's child gate (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/meme-backstop.ts`, `runChildGate`), which runs the ingest gate's READ HALF — `evaluateMeme`, never `placeMeme` — over the composed root and surfaces what it finds on the SAME alert rail the quoteblock uses: a second live ETX, `frame-malformed`, `postamble-content` at error grade, and, widened past that leg, a composed-altitude ahu balance fault (`ahu-unbalanced-open`, `ahu-orphan-close` — the dangling opener eating the parent's closer, or the orphan closing the parent early) that the gate's own NOOP-equivalence leg grades below error and would otherwise drop. This never lands or refuses anything on the stock syncer path; the root door gate's own ingest grades stand untouched.

!!! WHERE the floor sits ~ BUILT

''The whole-chunk floor runs inside the deserializer, directly after the frame `verdict()`'' — a pure,
idempotent text transform, so every door that reads a carrier fences by construction. No door carries
its own copy, and no door skips it. The order runs fixed:

# ''Frame verdict first.'' The frame reads before any grammar does (`packages/lararium-memetic-frame/src/verdict.ts`).
# ''A torn frame never decomposes.'' TiddlyWiki's deserializer contract runs synchronous, fields out, with no refuse channel — so the deserializer holds a torn carrier verbatim as ONE record (`text/plain`, the frame's faults on `$torn`), and the Confluence gate refuses it on the frame's own error grade. No fence repairs a tear: quoteblocking a torn frame would hide the tear inside a span that reads sound.
# ''Else decompose'' — the family split runs over the framed body.
# ''If any ERROR or MISSING node remains'' anywhere in that decomposition, ''the WHOLE chunk fences'' and the fence surfaces. A partial fence over only the faulted span stays forbidden at this grain: no family stands yet to hold the sound remainder.

''The seat.'' `quoteblockFloor` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/deserializer.ts`), laid by `memeticWikitextDeserializer` itself, reads each carrier's framed body through the family split's own machine reader — `scanAhu` over the fence mask, never the grammar: ONE stack whose top-level blocks the split cuts and whose balance faults the floor fences on — where an ERROR reads as `ahu-orphan-close` (a closer that closes nothing) and a MISSING as `ahu-unbalanced-open` (an opener whose closer never arrives). The head, the frame and the root meta stay outside the fence, a check that matched re-stamps over the fenced body, and the fenced root record carries `$quoteblocked` — the floor's own account of what it fenced and why (`$`-opening, so it never re-emits into the meta fence or moves the canonical render). A fenced body masks every sigil it holds, so a second pass finds nothing left to fence.

''One reading.'' The deserializer reads the frame's shape (`frameShape`) and takes its digest only where a fence lands, to decide whether a matching check re-stamps. Each carrier is divided and its ahu stack scanned ONCE, and that reading (`CarrierReading`) is what the floor, the split and the carrier check (`checkCarrier`) all read. The Confluence gate reads the frame verdict once and hands it to the family's `deserialize`, and reads the structure the disk declares off the text the floor already laid, never laying it twice.

''Every door, one fence.'' Each reads the carrier through that deserializer:

* the Confluence gate (`decideIngest`, through `deserializeCarrier`), and with it `placeMeme` on every door that places — the meme face, the `/memes/` routes, the syncer INGEST, the backstop — and `canonicalizeCarrierText` on the projecting leg;
* the bag doors: LOAD, a native single-carrier INGEST and each pack member, whenever TiddlyWiki's registry hands the bytes to the memetic type;
* TiddlyWiki's own doors — import, drag-drop, paste and the boot-folder load — through the registered `text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki` deserializer.

''Every door, surfaced.'' A fence nobody sees reads as a drop wearing a cure's face:

* ''a wiki sink'' raises the one alert rail (`surfaceMemeAlert`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/place-meme.ts`) the child gate shares;
* ''a bag door'' holds no rail, so its receipt carries the warning: LOAD's summary, the syncer INGEST's `ingest` receipt, a native INGEST's receipt and each pack member's own receipt — and a torn hold names its tear there too;
* ''import, drop and paste'' stage every record in `$:/Import` for the operator, and the `import-floor-upgrader` module (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/import-floor-upgrader.ts`) speaks beside each fenced or torn title in that listing — it unchecks nothing and edits nothing;
* ''the boot-folder load'' stages nothing for review; its fence and its torn hold surface on the record itself, through `$quoteblocked` and `$torn`.

Witness: `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/quoteblock-floor-ingest.test.ts` (the gate, the projecting leg, the backstop) and `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/quoteblock-floor-doors.test.ts` (the deserializer contract, every bag door, the import listing, a booted wiki).

''The stock syncer keeps NEVER-REFUSE.'' A child-slot save on the stock syncer path lands as written and only re-grades its root (the backstop paragraph above); the WHERE above governs the ingest gate's whole-chunk door and changes nothing about that path.

This law lifts [[graceful-parsing|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/graceful-parsing#/recovery-policy]]'s panic-to-water floor from Layer 1 (the meme-ast builder, one sigil) to Layer 2 (the family split, one ahu or one whole carrier): water never regresses, never lies about structure, and composes with repair added later.

<<~/ahu>>

